    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-047: CSS Mask Image**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~350 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Closes ADR-045's mask-image deferral.** ADR-045's measurement found 13 of 14 `background-size` rules target `mask-image` — this ADR adds the subsystem that makes those rules renderable.\n\n## Measurement (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-29)\n\n| Category | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Total `mask-*` rules | **127** |\n| Rules with `background-color` (fill present → renderable) | **14** |\n| Rules without `background-color` (companion fill rules) | 113 |\n| Data URL mask images (inline SVG/PNG) | 13 |\n| External SVG mask images | 1 |\n\n**Only 14 combinations have both mask + fill.** The other 113 rely on companion rules matching the same element.\n\n## First-viewport targets (honest assessment)\n\n| Selector | First-viewport | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`.cdx-message__icon`** | **✅ Visible** | Issue-box icon at y≈400 (verified by ADR-040/043 screenshots) |\n| `.cdx-search-input__start-icon` | ⚠️ Header-dependent | Needs ADR-029 flex layout |\n| `.vector-icon` (theme selector, hamburger) | ⚠️ Header-dependent | Same |\n| `.vector-dropdown-label::after` (chevron) | ⚠️ Header-dependent | Same |\n\n**3 of 4 renderable categories require ADR-029 header layout.** `.cdx-message__icon` is the only guaranteed first-viewport target.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Commit 1 — Parse + layout fields (behavior-neutral)\n- `LayoutBox` gains `mask_image_url`, `mask_size_w/h`, `mask_pos_x/y`, `mask_no_repeat`, `mask_has`\n- Parse `mask-image` / `-webkit-mask-image` (URL + data URL forms, both quoted and raw SVG)\n- Parse `mask-size` / `mask-position` / `mask-repeat`\n- Priority: unprefixed wins if both present\n- ~12 unit tests\n- Zero paint changes\n\n### Commit 2 — Paint (visible)\n- New `paint_mask_image()` using `cairo_mask_surface`\n- `paint_box` calls it after background fill, before border (correct CSS order)\n- **PNG verification gate before merge**\n- Primary target: `.cdx-message__icon` (first-viewport)\n- Header icons may appear once ADR-029 completes\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs\n- ADR-047 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-047 notes in ADR-034 (bg vs mask subsystems), ADR-045 (deferral closed)\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Design decisions worth flagging\n\n- [ ] **`cairo_mask_surface` after fill** — masks the current source (bg-color) through the surface's alpha. Single call, exactly CSS semantics.\n- [ ] **v1 renders only when `background_color.a > 0`** — elements with mask but no fill (via color inheritance) deferred. Transparent bg makes mask invisible anyway; no visual artifact. Documented deviation.\n- [ ] **Both `background-image` and `mask-image` can render simultaneously** — different CSS subsystems; both paint.\n- [ ] **`-webkit-mask-*` prefixes accepted** — many Wikipedia rules set both for browser compat. Unprefixed wins if both present.\n- [ ] **Honest scope: 3 of 4 targets header-dependent** — only `.cdx-message__icon` guaranteed visible. If that element doesn't render as expected, delta is 0. Documented upfront per ADR-041/044/045 discipline.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `mask-mode: luminance` (0 uses; SVG masks are alpha)\n- `mask-composite`, `mask-border`, `mask-clip`, `mask-origin`\n- Percentage `mask-size` / `mask-position`\n- `mask-repeat: repeat | repeat-x | repeat-y` (0 uses)\n- Elements with mask but no `background-color` fill\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 586 / 2263 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/047-mask-image.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #223\n",
